# React Patterns (apps/web)

## Styling

**BaseUI + CSS Modules — no Tailwind, no shadcn/ui.**

- Use [Base UI](https://base-ui.com) for unstyled/accessible primitives (dialogs, dropdowns, popovers, etc.)
- Style with CSS Modules: one `ComponentName.module.css` file per component
- Import styles as `styles` and apply via `className={styles.foo}`
- Never use inline style objects except for dynamic computed values (e.g. calculated widths)

```typescript
import styles from './SpecCard.module.css';

export function SpecCard({ spec }: SpecCardProps) {
  return (
    <div className={styles.card}>
      <span className={styles.title}>{spec.title}</span>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Component Conventions

**Named function exports — no default exports:**

```typescript
// CORRECT
export function BacklogView() {
  return <div>...</div>;
}

// WRONG
export default function BacklogView() { ... }
const BacklogView = () => { ... }; export default BacklogView;
```

**Props type with `Props` suffix:**

```typescript
type SpecCardProps = {
  spec: Spec;
  onRefine?: () => void;
  className?: string;
};

export function SpecCard({ spec, onRefine, className }: SpecCardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

## File Organization

```
apps/web/src/
  routes/              # TanStack Start file-based routes
    __root.tsx         # Root layout (providers)
    login.tsx          # /login (unauthenticated — placeholder)
    onboarding.tsx     # /onboarding (first-run — placeholder, shape TBD)
    _auth.tsx          # App-shell layout — requires auth + a workspace; left rail + Settings gear
    _auth/
      index.tsx        # / → Today (dashboard)
      backlog.tsx      # /backlog route (Specs/Actions/Blockers as in-page views)
      schedule.tsx     # /schedule route (week/month as in-page views)
      insights.tsx     # /insights route (v1: Performance only; more tabs post-v1)
      specs.$specId.tsx  # /specs/$specId — spec detail (overlay over the current page in-app; standalone when cold-loaded)
      settings/        # /settings/* (sub-pages TBD)
      tray.tsx         # /tray route (desktop tray window — loaded by Tauri; not a nav item)
  components/
    shared/            # Reusable across features
    today/             # Today-specific components
    backlog/           # Backlog-specific components
    schedule/          # Schedule-specific components
    insights/          # Insights-specific components
    specs/             # Spec view + the ad-hoc spec modal
    tray/              # Tray-specific components
  hooks/               # Custom hooks (useAuth.ts, useQueue.ts)
  lib/                 # Non-React utilities
```

## Route Files — TanStack Start

Each route file exports a `Route` created with `createFileRoute`:

```typescript
// routes/_auth/backlog.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router';
import { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { client } from '@stride/api-client';

const specsQueryOptions = queryOptions({
  queryKey: ['specs'],
  queryFn: () => client.specs.$get().then(r => r.json()),
});

export const Route = createFileRoute('/_auth/backlog')({
  loader: ({ context: { queryClient } }) =>
    queryClient.ensureQueryData(specsQueryOptions),
  component: BacklogView,
});

function BacklogView() {
  const specs = Route.useLoaderData();
  return <div>...</div>;
}
```

**Rules:**
- Loaders prefetch data server-side (web SSR) or client-side (desktop SPA) — same code, different runtime
- Use `queryClient.ensureQueryData` in loaders so TanStack Query cache is always primed
- Components read from cache via `useSuspenseQuery` — never fetch in components directly
- Route component is a named function defined in the same file, not exported separately

## Data Fetching — TanStack Query

**All server state lives in TanStack Query:**

```typescript
import { useSuspenseQuery, useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { client } from '@stride/api-client';

export function SpecList() {
  const { data: specs } = useSuspenseQuery({
    queryKey: ['specs'],
    queryFn: () => client.specs.$get().then(r => r.json()),
  });

  return <ul>{specs.map(spec => <SpecCard key={spec.id} spec={spec} />)}</ul>;
}
```

**Mutations go through the queue abstraction:**

```typescript
import { useQueueMutation } from '@/hooks/useQueueMutation';
import { client } from '@stride/api-client';

export function RefineSpec({ specId }: { specId: string }) {
  const mutation = useQueueMutation({
    mutationFn: (input: AddActionInput) =>
      client.specs[':id'].actions.$post({ param: { id: specId }, json: input }),
    optimisticUpdate: (cache, input) => {
      // update TanStack Query cache optimistically
    },
  });

  return <button onClick={() => mutation.mutate({ title: 'New action' })}>Add action</button>;
}
```

**Rules:**
- `useSuspenseQuery` for reads (wrap route in `<Suspense>`)
- `useQuery` only when you need the loading/error state inline
- Never fetch in `useEffect` — use loaders or query hooks
- Always specify `queryKey` arrays that fully describe the query's dependencies
- Mutations use `useQueueMutation` (wraps `useMutation` + offline queue) — not raw `useMutation`

## State Management

| State type | Where it lives |
|---|---|
| Server/API data | TanStack Query (`useSuspenseQuery`) |
| Ephemeral UI state | `useState` (modal open, form inputs, hover) |
| Cross-component UI state | React Context (`src/lib/context/`) |
| Form state | TanStack Form |
| Offline queue state | `packages/queue` via `useQueueStatus` hook |

## Forms — TanStack Form

```typescript
import { useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form';
import { z } from 'zod';

const schema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1, 'Title is required'),
  estimate: z.number().positive().optional(),
});

export function AddActionForm({ onSubmit }: { onSubmit: (v: z.infer<typeof schema>) => void }) {
  const form = useForm({
    defaultValues: { title: '', estimate: undefined },
    validators: { onChange: schema },
    onSubmit: ({ value }) => onSubmit(value),
  });

  return (
    <form onSubmit={e => { e.preventDefault(); form.handleSubmit(); }}>
      <form.Field name="title">
        {field => (
          <input
            value={field.state.value}
            onChange={e => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
          />
        )}
      </form.Field>
    </form>
  );
}
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
// Route-level error boundary
export const Route = createFileRoute('/_auth/backlog')({
  errorComponent: ({ error }) => <ErrorView error={error} />,
  component: BacklogView,
});

// In components
try {
  await mutation.mutateAsync(input);
} catch (err) {
  if (isApiError(err, 422)) {
    setFieldError(err.field, err.message);
  } else if (isApiError(err, 403)) {
    setError("You don't have access");
  } else {
    throw err; // bubble to nearest ErrorBoundary
  }
}
```

## Custom Hooks

```typescript
// src/hooks/useAuth.ts
export function useAuth() {
  const context = useContext(AuthContext);
  if (!context) throw new Error('useAuth must be used within AuthProvider');
  return context;
}
```

- All custom hooks live in `src/hooks/`
- Hooks wrapping a context always throw if used outside the provider
- Named `useSomething` — always camelCase with `use` prefix
